{%- comment -%}
  FUEL_06 product page gate. Prints "true" when the finder belongs on this
  product page, nothing otherwise. One rule for the dialog (layout/theme.liquid)
  and the link under the buy button (snippets/fuel06-pdp-link.liquid), so the
  two can never disagree.

  On when: the "Show on product pages" setting is on and the product's template
  suffix is in the "Product templates" setting (comma separated, e.g.
  "qunatity-breaks,expressive-notes"). Bundle templates are left out of that
  list, so bundle pages load no finder CSS, JS or markup.

  Usage:
  {%- capture f06_pdp -%}{%- render 'fuel06-pdp-enabled' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- if f06_pdp == 'true' -%} ... {%- endif -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if request.page_type == 'product' and settings.fuel06_pdp_enabled
    assign f06_suffix = template.suffix | default: '' | strip
    assign f06_templates = settings.fuel06_pdp_templates | split: ','
    for f06_t in f06_templates
      assign f06_clean = f06_t | strip
      if f06_clean != blank and f06_clean == f06_suffix
        echo 'true'
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
